fix(dashboard): close the facts strip instead of orphaning its last cell

Measured in a browser on a real run. Nine facts in a four-column grid put
REPOSITORIES alone on the third row beside three empty cells, which reads as
missing data rather than as the end of the strip.

A Fact may now take the whole row, and the repositories cell does. Eight facts
fill two rows exactly; the ninth closes the strip instead of hanging off it.

No test drove this and none could have: every assertion about the strip is
about which facts it carries and what they are called, and all of those still
hold. What changed is the shape of an area no assertion describes, which is the
gap a rendered check exists to cover (doc 06 P4). The full suite is green
either way, and that is the point worth recording rather than hiding.

